Line counts (surface = page + co-located components, well-decomposed per ADR-002):
  SearchPage.kt 451 · SearchPageIcons.kt 213 · SearchPageModel.kt 155 · SearchPageViewModel.kt 122 ·
  SearchPageSource.kt 52 · SearchPageHost.kt 48  => 1041 lines for the surface vs the 279-line web page
  (web SearchPage.tsx). Comprehensive, not gutted; far above the 70% floor.

Data   : SearchPageViewModel owns the live SearchInput (query + the active type filter + the per-type limit=25) and
         plans every input through the shared core `planSearch` gate (the web hook's `enabled` guard). An enabled
         query streams cache-then-network through SearchPageSource.search -> the shared S7
         SearchRepository.globalSearch (web `useGlobalSearch`'s queryFn: GET /search?q=&types=&limit=); a too-short /
         empty query settles to empty hits WITHOUT a request (skipSearchResults; web `enabled: false`). The flat
         hits are grouped into per-type sections in display order by groupHits (the web `groupedHits` memo, which
         lives in the PAGE, not the hook), folded into UiState via searchResultsResource preserving every freshness
         flag. No HTTP in the view.
Adapt  : the web page's per-row timestamp is `<TimeStamp …className="hidden … sm:inline"/>` — hidden at the mobile
         breakpoint — so it is intentionally NOT rendered on this phone surface (faithful to the web's small-screen
         render). The web `AINLSearch` (opt-in natural-language box) returns null whenever ai_mode is 'off' (the
         default install) and is not a declared parity item, so it is not ported.
Strings: all 22 page keys ALREADY present in res/values/strings.xml + values-ar + values-he (generated by
         apps/shared/i18n) — no string-catalog edit needed; every literal resolves via
         stringResource(R.string.translation_search_*). search.noResults.message carries the `%1$s` query slot.
Nav    : Destinations 'search' -> /search pre-existing (Destinations.kt:180, NavGroup.Search; count unchanged); host
         wired via PageHosts.register; each result row opens hit.url through the app's own teslasync://app deep-link
         scheme (AndroidManifest + TeslaSyncNavHost, web `navigate(hit.url)`) since no NavController is exposed to
         page hosts.

